{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1092063-concern-for-the-future-of-chronicles","id":1092063,"title":"Concern for The Future of Chronicles","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-05-13T12:58:14-07:00","id":1092063,"title":"Concern for The Future of Chronicles","content":"As we are all aware, White Wolf is making a very big push to let the world know that not only is VtM5e a thing that's coming out in the very near future, but they're bringing back the old World of Darkness. For us fans of tabletop RPGs where you play spooky-scaries, this is obviously great news.<br /> <br /> However, it's got me wondering about the future of the Chronicles of Darkness.<br /> <br /> I know Onyx Path is licensed out to create the CofD games and supplements (and we all think you guys do a bang-up job and we all love you!), but as I understand it, at the end of the day White Wolf still owns the property. Would they be willing to keep both lines going and essentially not only compete with themselves, but potentially add confusion among newcomers who don't know there's two very different Werewolf/Vampire/Mage/Changeling/etc. games owned by the same company?<br /> <br /> I can only hope so. I openly admit that while I like both lines, I much prefer the smoother mechanics and treatment of horror within the CofD. And having purchased and read the main 2e books, i love how much work Onyx Path has put into further differentiatibg between the CofD and WoD. At the same time, though, I notice CofD is updating the rest of the line to 2e and working on Deviants, but there doesn't seem to be a lot of upcoming supplements for the lines. Meanwhile, my social media is regularly reminding me of CtD20, the cool-looking VtM card game, visual novels for VtM and MtAw, and whatever new supplement has been released for WtA or VtM.<br /> <br /> Maybe I'm just reading too much into it. After all, what long-time tabletop fan *hasn't* had a bunch of grumbles over changes to new editions and such? It could be that White Wolf really wants a push to promote WoD before they kick off the relaunch with VtM5e, and next year Onyx Path plans on giving us so many CofD supplements we won't know what to do with them all (read them, would be my first guess).<br /> <br /> In any case, here I stand, looking at an uncertain future.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":13448,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13448-gorillacannon","user":"GorillaCannon","date":". 05-13-2017, 04:01 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13448-gorillacannon","name":"GorillaCannon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-13T13:09:16-07:00","id":1092066,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GorillaCannon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1092063-concern-for-the-future-of-chronicles#post1092063\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I know Onyx Path is licensed out to create the CofD games and supplements (and we all think you guys do a bang-up job and we all love you!), but as I understand it, at the end of the day White Wolf still owns the property. Would they be willing to keep both lines going and essentially not only compete with themselves, but potentially add confusion among newcomers who don't know there's two very different Werewolf/Vampire/Mage/Changeling/etc. games owned by the same company?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think that's part of the reason behind the name change to Chronicles. RichT and others have spoken, however, and there doesn't seem to be any intent to kill the line. From an economic standpoint it's making everyone money, and it might be seen as a 'gateway' game for old World of Darkness stuff. I'm concerned too, of course, but so far it looks like if it's going to happen we're not going to get any warning about it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I can only hope so. I openly admit that while I like both lines, I much prefer the smoother mechanics and treatment of horror within the CofD. And having purchased and read the main 2e books, i love how much work Onyx Path has put into further differentiatibg between the CofD and WoD. At the same time, though, I notice CofD is updating the rest of the line to 2e and working on Deviants, but there doesn't seem to be a lot of upcoming supplements for the lines. Meanwhile, my social media is regularly reminding me of CtD20, the cool-looking VtM card game, visual novels for VtM and MtAw, and whatever new supplement has been released for WtA or VtM. </div> </div> </div>Outside of the visual novels, that all seems to be Onyx Path stuff. I'm hoping we get more Chronicles work done once White Wolf starts publishing their own stuff but they've put out a lot of Chronicles supplements. Just last month we had Night Horrors: Conquering Heroes, Cursed Necropolis: Rio, and some of the individual Dark Eras, while the only old World of Darkness supplement to come out was Lore of the Bloodlines.<br /> <br /> We've had threads like this before, you might do some searching for official responses to them. They basically happen after every major announcement from White Wolf.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-13T13:11:07-07:00","id":1092067,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GorillaCannon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1092063-concern-for-the-future-of-chronicles#post1092063\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I know Onyx Path is licensed out to create the CofD games and supplements (and we all think you guys do a bang-up job and we all love you!), but as I understand it, at the end of the day White Wolf still owns the property. Would they be willing to keep both lines going and essentially not only compete with themselves, but potentially add confusion among newcomers who don't know there's two very different Werewolf/Vampire/Mage/Changeling/etc. games owned by the same company?</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean...there's a reason why it got re-branded from &quot;New World of Darkness&quot; to &quot;Chronicles of Darkness&quot;.<br /> <br /> Pretty sure things will be fine.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-13T14:44:34-07:00","id":1092106,"title":"","content":"Well with the amount of freelance writers boycotting nuWw I don't think we have to worry about talent drain <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13009-burritomage","name":"BurritoMage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13009_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"585"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-13T14:47:48-07:00","id":1092108,"title":"","content":"From everything Rich, Rose, and even the people at the new WW have said, it truly doesn't seem like there's any intent to cancel the line. There are numerous CofD books in development (both announced and yet-to-be announced), and, as no father pointed out, the whole point of the name change was to differentiate the Worlds of Darkness so that there wouldn't be as much confusion. Tabletop is only one part of the transmedia effort new WW is putting together, and it's presumably not the one they're putting the most money into. This is just my two cents, but I doubt they would've gone to the effort of rebranding and approving new books if they were just planning to cancel it in the nebulous future.<br /> <br /> I completely appreciate your fear, and I'll admit I had it myself when there was uncertainty over what was going to happen with the new IP owners, but it really isn't productive to worry about the sky falling until someone actually says it is. I have my issues with the new WW's direction, but they've been open about what they want to do with CofD, which is ultimately that they don't want to screw with it; it's OPP's baby. Rose has also said that the high quality of the second editions influenced that decision.<br /> <br /> (I seem to remember a Swedish forum member randomly had, like, tea with Martin Ericsson to ask him about this very issue...?)<br /> <br /> tl;dr: As things stand, there really isn't anything to worry about.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-13T17:29:14-07:00","id":1092166,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1092063-concern-for-the-future-of-chronicles?p=1092066#post1092066\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think that's part of the reason behind the name change to Chronicles. RichT and others have spoken, however, and there doesn't seem to be any intent to kill the line. From an economic standpoint it's making everyone money, and it might be seen as a 'gateway' game for old World of Darkness stuff. I'm concerned too, of course, but so far it looks like if it's going to happen we're not going to get any warning about it.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Outside of the visual novels, that all seems to be Onyx Path stuff. I'm hoping we get more Chronicles work done once White Wolf starts publishing their own stuff but they've put out a lot of Chronicles supplements. Just last month we had Night Horrors: Conquering Heroes, Cursed Necropolis: Rio, and some of the individual Dark Eras, while the only old World of Darkness supplement to come out was Lore of the Bloodlines.<br /> <br /> We've had threads like this before, you might do some searching for official responses to them. They basically happen after every major announcement from White Wolf.</div> </div> </div> </div> Yes! Without having to share resources with OWOD, the CoD will get more attention and hopefully more products released. <br /> <br /> It's fans of OWOD that need to be concerned, so far I've seen some seriously unhappy OWOD fans.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-13T17:43:44-07:00","id":1092168,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yossarian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1092063-concern-for-the-future-of-chronicles?p=1092108#post1092108\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">From everything Rich, Rose, and even the people at the new WW have said, it truly doesn't seem like there's any intent to cancel the line. There are numerous CofD books in development (both announced and yet-to-be announced), and, as no father pointed out, the whole point of the name change was to differentiate the Worlds of Darkness so that there wouldn't be as much confusion. Tabletop is only one part of the transmedia effort new WW is putting together, and it's presumably not the one they're putting the most money into. This is just my two cents, but I doubt they would've gone to the effort of rebranding and approving new books if they were just planning to cancel it in the nebulous future.<br /> <br /> I completely appreciate your fear, and I'll admit I had it myself when there was uncertainty over what was going to happen with the new IP owners, but it really isn't productive to worry about the sky falling until someone actually says it is. I have my issues with the new WW's direction, but they've been open about what they want to do with CofD, which is ultimately that they don't want to screw with it; it's OPP's baby. Rose has also said that the high quality of the second editions influenced that decision.<br /> <br /> (I seem to remember a Swedish forum member randomly had, like, tea with Martin Ericsson to ask him about this very issue...?)<br /> <br /> tl;dr: As things stand, there really isn't anything to worry about.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not Martin. Martin's the Creative Director. I think it was with the CEO of nuWW. <br /> <br /> Anyhow, as others have said, CofD will be fine. The two gamelines are distinct despite their common origins, they seem to appeal to different targets, and nuWW seems to want to have a very different aesthetic in mind for oWod.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-15T12:48:26-07:00","id":1092919,"title":"","content":"We're working on a bunch of CofD stuff, with more on deck after it. WWP has been nothing but positive about what we've been doing, and nobody has floated canceling the line in even the vaguest sense.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Cavaliers of Mars Creator</b><br /> <b>Retired CofD Lead</b><br /> <br /> Check out my <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Rose%20Bailey\" target=\"_blank\">guides to </a><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/261142/BITE-ME-How-to-Write-Vampire?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> and my <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse/pub/4895/Fantasy-Heartbreaker?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">indie games</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2-rose-bailey","name":"Rose Bailey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2361"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-15T14:27:21-07:00","id":1092957,"title":"","content":"I'm a little confused at what you mean by OP having no new stuff coming out for their gamelines. There are a ton of stuff in the works from what the Monday Meeting Notes have said: <br /> <br /> - Thousand Years of Night (VtR)<br /> <br /> - Building a Legend (BtP)<br /> <br /> - Sign &amp; Sorcery (MtAw)<br /> <br /> - Beast Player's Guide (BtP)<br /> <br /> - Night Horrors: Enemy Action (DtD)<br /> <br /> - Anthologies for CtL &amp; HtV<br /> <br /> - And of course 2nd Edition Core Books for CtL, HtV, and GtSE. <br /> <br /> And that's just the stuff they've mentioned in the works. Who knows what other projects they have on the back burner. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage","name":"Dusksage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3436_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-04T07:47:58-07:00","id":1100121,"title":"","content":"Well we know they plan on releasing a book called The Hedge after CtL corebook.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-04T17:07:59-07:00","id":1100267,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1092063-concern-for-the-future-of-chronicles?p=1100121#post1100121\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well we know they plan on releasing a book called The Hedge after CtL corebook.</div> </div> </div> </div>Are they? It hasn't been mentioned since Rose took over CtL and it's disappeared from the signatures of people like ArcaneArts.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-04T19:22:21-07:00","id":1100293,"title":"","content":"The third books, outside of vampire, seem to have stop being pushed, by which I mean, they aren't talking about them in public as far as I can tell. Werewolf had a Secrets of the Tribes announced in one brochure, and Mage had a Secrets of the Orders or Pentacle or something. They may still be being worked on, but we were told that not everyone's going to get a book every year, so it may just be about how many projects they can have open to however many developers, writers, and so forth that they have.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-04T23:48:12-07:00","id":1100354,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>milo v3</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1092063-concern-for-the-future-of-chronicles?p=1100267#post1100267\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Are they? It hasn't been mentioned since Rose took over CtL and it's disappeared from the signatures of people like ArcaneArts.</div> </div> </div> </div>Is it?<br /> <br /> The Hedge is still on the Current Projects tab, but admittedly has not shown up in the MMNs. And I believe when Rose first put up the &quot;A Walk in the Hedge&quot; Open Dev post, among the comments she mentioned how there's a reason the Hedge is getting its' own book, which would naturally mean the book is still getting made. Maybe the writers originally on got pulled/shuffled around due to the change in developer and thus direction?<br /> <br /> Or just putting that book on hold until CtL2e actually gets released or is close to release.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1092063-concern-for-the-future-of-chronicles?p=1100293#post1100293\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The third books, outside of vampire, seem to have stop being pushed, by which I mean, they aren't talking about them in public as far as I can tell. Werewolf had a Secrets of the Tribes announced in one brochure, and <b>Mage had a Secrets of the Orders or Pentacle or something.</b> They may still be being worked on, but we were told that not everyone's going to get a book every year, so it may just be about how many projects they can have open to however many developers, writers, and so forth that they have.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's Tome of the Pentacle. Which like The Hedge, is in the Current Projects tab but not in the MMNs. But in its' case, wasn't there problems on Dave Brookshaw's end that prevented him with moving forward with some of the MtAw2e books? Hence why Deviant's been slow to get started and why Signs of Sorcery has been perpetually stuck in Development stage?<br /> <br /> Although I'll give you &quot;Secrets of the Tribes&quot; being mysteriously absent. And PtC2e having no books listed or hinted at period.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4418,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","user":"tasti man LH","date":". 06-05-2017, 03:36 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-05T00:23:22-07:00","id":1100362,"title":"","content":"A Clarification since I got mentioned: My &quot;contract&quot; for The Hedge was more of a very early employment promise from David Hill-at the time, CtL 2E had been announced, and was, I think, in the middle of his collection of first drafts. Around Autumn of last year, David said he was soon going to be gearing up for The Hedge and asked for word count commitments from people-I made my bid.<br /> <br /> That was half a year before the change in leadership was announced, relatively speaking. Since then, I've been busy, so I haven't been able to ask about my involvement with The Hedge(and on top of that I think I have the wrong e-mail for Rose), so I erred on the side of caution and assumed since there wasn't a contract at that point I couldn't safely speak to my involvement with the project. Or, more simply put, now in a situation without a promise, I figured I wasn't on it until I had a contract.<br /> <br /> My intention with removing it from my project list was not to suggest that The Hedge was not going through-while I don't have any for-sure knowledge beyond what is shared by Richard and Rose in the blogs and on the forums, I also didn't have any particular doubts that it would still be the next supplement. I apologize for the confusion that may have incited.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Pre-empting some possible questions- No, I dunno what's going on with my material for the core, Yes, I will ask and when I know and if it's appropriate to share I will let you know what's happening there, and Yes, this entire thing is complicated, let's not make a discussion about it right now.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 06-05-2017, 03:33 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-05T02:35:13-07:00","id":1100379,"title":"","content":"Slightly off-topic, but I feel the need to share <a href=\"https://mythcreants.com/b